{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit change 3421 patch set 1: LLM-Review +1, Verified -1. The only failure was my new test `test_calibrate_criterion_opens_a_gate_session_for_its_solver`, which called `calibrate_criterion(\"G7\")`; on the case-sensitive ubuntu runners `plan-review-G7.eval.yaml` does not exist (the file is `plan-review-g7.eval.yaml`). Switched the test to the `necessity` criterion (filename matches its prompt) and amended. The filename/prompt mismatch is a separate pre-existing defect that would also abort the eval-live loop on Linux at G7: filed as militant-vixenish-gorilla (discovered_from this ticket)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794978451546921963,"uuid":"cf5a2f5b-ce6f-4f52-9d25-efff4f9b2c0f"}